module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_positive_control_certifies_the_defect_it_exists_to_catch

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data a_positive_control_certifies_the_defect_it_exists_to_catch: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_positive_control_certifies_the_defect_it_exists_to_catch" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**A POSITIVE CONTROL IS EXACTLY WHERE NOBODY CHECKS THE SUBJECT, BECAUSE THE ASSERTION PASSING IS READ AS THE SUBJECT BEING RIGHT.** A negative control is interrogated: it is expected to red, so when it greens somebody asks why. A positive control is expected to green, and it does, so the question never forms. The failure is therefore invisible in exactly proportion to how trusted the control is - and the control that proves an accessor works is the most trusted artifact in a module. The defect is not a wrong row: a wrong row is ordinary and gets found. It is that the instrument pointed at the row reports agreement with it, so the row and its check are wrong TOGETHER and no disagreement is available to anyone.",

    "SPECIMEN ONE (2026-09-09, gunbc colo census, corridor lane). `databank_lga4_density` published \"35kW+\" - a capability FLOOR - in a carrier whose only figure-bearing arms are MAXIMA. The census's own positive control asserted `established_watts == 35000` and a refusal at 35,001 W. The operator ruling that demoted the row recorded what the control had actually established: \"it proved instead that nobody had checked what the row said\".",

    "SPECIMEN TWO AND THREE (2026-09-10, same census, session bright-swift-678, found by reading the corridor lane's demotion rather than by any check of this lane's own). `w_central_nj_read_densities_are_their_published_watts` asserted established readings of 16,000 / 15,000 / 10,000 W across three rows. TWO of those three were capability floors: `databank_ewr2_density` carries the same \"10kW+\" wording as the specimen above, and `digital_fortress_piscataway_density` was ruled `CapabilityAtLeast`. A consumer asking whether 10,001 W was refused got YES from a page promising AT LEAST 10 kW, under a green control named for reading published watts. BOTH ROWS' CITATIONS ALREADY CONTAINED THE REFUTATION IN PROSE - \"the plus sign is the operator's own, so the integer is a marketed floor rather than a ceiling\" - beside the typed value that contradicted it.",

    "SPECIMEN FOUR (2026-09-09, the density carrier itself). A re-keyed witness asked a question the carrier refuses by construction, so it was permanently green and carried no information - the decoration DESIGN section 4b rules worse than absent, because it is cited as coverage. Four specimens, three lanes, one night, and in every case the author of the control was not the finder.",

    "SPECIMEN FIVE (2026-09-10, the carrier's own merge, and it carries a DISTINCT MECHANISM worth the separate entry: TRANSLATING A CONTROL ACROSS A CARRIER CHANGE IS ITSELF A SUBJECT-CHECK-SKIPPING MOVE). Resolving a conflict, the carrier author re-keyed another lane's conjunct `established_watts(iron_mountain_nje1_density) == 30000` into an outside-maximum query against `AirCooling`. That reads as a faithful translation and is not one: NJE-1's page names NO cooling medium, so an air-keyed request finds no figure and the screen refuses for ABSENCE rather than for the ceiling. The pre-migration inference that an unlabelled figure answers an air question was reintroduced INSIDE the change that exists to delete it, while translating a witness away from a different instance of this same class. The translator's attention is on preserving the assertion's SHAPE, and the shape survives intact while the subject silently stops supporting it - so a translation inherits the original's trust without inheriting its subject.",

    "**RECOGNITION RULE: for each positive control, ask what it would assert if its SUBJECT were wrong in the way the surrounding type permits.** If the answer is \"the same thing\", the control is measuring the accessor and not the row, and the row is unchecked. Two mechanical tells, both cheap: a control whose subject row carries HEDGING PROSE in its citation - \"floor\", \"at least\", \"up to\", \"on request\", \"not a standing\", \"we could not\" - while the typed value is unhedged; and a control that reads a number BACK OUT of a carrier rather than probing a boundary, since reading back out can only agree with whatever the arm holds. THIRD TELL, FROM SPECIMEN FIVE: any control RE-KEYED across a carrier change, where the reviewer is comparing the new assertion to the old one rather than to the row - a re-keyed control must be EXECUTED before the commit that re-keys it, which is the cheap rule specimen five violated.",

    "DISTINCT FROM ITS NEIGHBOURS. A vacuous predicate is true over degenerate input and stays type-valid when the input turns real; this control is NOT vacuous - it executes, reads a real row, and returns a real true. A mutation that reds nothing is the absence of discrimination; here discrimination exists but is pointed at the accessor rather than at the claim. And rung inflation is a false claim ABOUT a guarantee; this is a true claim about a wrong subject, which is why no amount of re-reading the control's own text finds it.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable, and the containment is a sibling lane happening to read a neighbour's demotion commit. Nothing prevented it, the compiler accepted it, every gate was green, and the discovery path in all four specimens was a human reading a different lane's diff.",

    "CEILING: mechanically preventable, and not higher - the derivation matters. Whether a control's subject could be wrong in a type-permitted way is decidable from the carrier (enumerate the arms the subject's type admits, re-evaluate the assertion under each, and refuse a control whose verdict is invariant across arms that differ materially). But WHICH arm a source actually licenses is an external fact about a published page, outside the modeled guarantee, so construction cannot make the wrong subject unwritable. A mutation harness over the subject's arms is the wall; it is validation, and validation is the honest ceiling here.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: an arm-substitution mutation pass over every positive control - for each control, re-evaluate it with its subject row rebound to each other arm of its declared type, and refuse the control if its verdict does not change for at least one materially different arm. This is not satisfied by a per-witness mutation run by an author on the rows they chose, which is the current state and is what failed four times; it requires the substitution to be EXHAUSTIVE OVER THE TYPE and run by the gate rather than by the lane. The pass subsumes specimen five without a separate mechanism: NJE-1's verdict does not vary across its medium arms because no arm answers, which is exactly the invariance the pass refuses.",

    "WHY IT RANKS: the artifact this corrupts is the one cited when anyone asks whether a reading is trustworthy, so a single instance launders every row it touches. In this census it kept two unusable figures in the candidate set for two days and would have shipped them into a fleet-sizing decision, since the whole point of the density axis is deciding whether a 650 W-per-node fleet fits in a cabinet somebody will actually sell.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
